Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer, New Grad* position with *IXL Learning*. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience and a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, where I graduated with a 4.0 GPA. I am especially drawn to the opportunity to build the back-end wiring, application logic, and UI behind products used by students and teachers around the world.

At Sperse, I built those product layers end to end for a CRM workflow platform serving more than 10,000 users. Using Python, FastAPI, TypeScript, and React, I developed the application logic and UI that let users create, run, and monitor durable workflows. I owned features through design, coding, testing, debugging, and tuning; integrated Temporal with Valkey/Redis for reliable progress tracking; and built CI/CD pipelines with trace-based tests that caught latency, accuracy, and safety regressions before production. This combination of programming, analytical reasoning, and full-cycle ownership would let me contribute quickly to IXL's fast-paced development process.

Previously, at Qualitest, I designed a cloud-agnostic Storage Service in Java and Spring Boot with SQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, and AWS. It handled uploads, downloads, and deletions across S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO through expiring signed URLs. I also tuned PostgreSQL queries and built React and JavaScript visualizations for cross-functional stakeholders, then improved error recovery for 100K+ weekly executions with AWS Step Functions and Lambda. That work strengthened my ability to work both independently and with a wide variety of teams while translating user needs into reliable product features.

IXL's mission to improve learning for all by applying technology in thoughtful and innovative ways strongly resonates with me. I would be proud to help develop audaciously great, customer-focused products that give educators and students simple, intuitive ways to teach and learn more effectively. IXL's values of passion, tenacity, authenticity, kindness, and open collaboration are also the kind of engineering culture in which I do my best work.

I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience building application logic, user interfaces, and AWS-backed systems can support IXL Learning's mission. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

